        "url": "https://github.com/ros/geometry_tutorials/blob/8e677416092ac97606a4a23256c815ba2fe762d4/LICENSE",
        "scope": "Selected file has an Apache-2.0 header, copyright 2021 Open Source Robotics Foundation, Inc., plus a quaternion helper derived from transforms3d under BSD-2-Clause, copyright 2009-2019 Matthew Brett and Christoph Gohlke. Both notice sets apply to their components; retain attribution, terms, disclaimers and applicable notices when redistributing. Pinned BSD terms: https://github.com/matthew-brett/transforms3d/blob/f185e866ecccb66c545559bc9f2e19cb5025e0ab/LICENSE . This is not a choice between licenses or blanket package/dependency clearance.",
        "verified": true
      },
      "role": "installed_ROS2_console_script_node_without_main_guard",
      "invocation": {
        "entrypoint": "ros2 run turtle_tf2_py turtle_tf2_broadcaster",
        "notes": "Installed ROS 2 console command backed by the pinned setup.py registration turtle_tf2_py.turtle_tf2_broadcaster:main. The source defines main without a __main__ guard; direct python-file execution is not the declared node invocation. Starting the console entrypoint initializes rclpy and broadcasts transforms from incoming pose messages. The Hub supplies inert source metadata with no preparation/execution adapter and ran no ROS node, package installer or simulator. A single fetched Python file is insufficient."
      },
      "requirements_and_source_effects": "The package is labeled version 0.7.0 at a Rolling-branch source pin; neither label establishes a tested ROS distribution, Python version or operating system. The turtlename parameter defaults to turtle. Pose callbacks subscribe to /<turtlename>/pose, stamp transforms with current node time, set parent frame world and child frame turtlename, copy x/y with z=0, convert yaw to quaternion and call sendTransform. Set intended parameters and provide matching pose publishers; this node alone does not create a complete following demo. The exact source imports turtlesim_msgs, whose availability must be resolved in the chosen environment. The copied helper's pinned transforms3d terms were reviewed, but mathematical correctness, clock/frame behavior, package installation and ROS graph compatibility were not executed or tested."
    },
    {
      "id": "ros2-tf2-listener",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/ros/geometry_tutorials",
