      "license": {
        "spdx": "Apache-2.0",
        "url": "https://github.com/ros/geometry_tutorials/blob/8e677416092ac97606a4a23256c815ba2fe762d4/LICENSE",
        "scope": "Selected listener source under its explicit Apache-2.0 header, copyright 2021 Open Source Robotics Foundation, Inc. Preserve attribution, license and applicable notices. The package also declares BSD for other material; this source review does not clear the full package, dependencies or physical-robot use.",
        "verified": true
      },
      "role": "installed_ROS2_console_script_node_without_main_guard",
      "invocation": {
        "entrypoint": "ros2 run turtle_tf2_py turtle_tf2_listener",
        "notes": "Installed ROS 2 console command backed by the pinned setup.py registration turtle_tf2_py.turtle_tf2_listener:main. The source defines main without a __main__ guard; direct python-file execution is not the declared node invocation. Starting the console entrypoint initializes rclpy, calls a spawn service and can publish velocity commands to the configured graph. No physical-controller compatibility or safe stopping is established. The Hub supplies inert source metadata with no preparation/execution adapter and ran no ROS node or simulator."
      },
      "requirements_and_source_effects": "The package is labeled version 0.7.0 at a Rolling-branch source pin; neither label establishes a tested ROS distribution, Python version or operating system. The node defaults target_frame to turtle1, requests turtle2 at x=4.0, y=2.0, theta=0.0 and, after spawning, queries a transform into turtle2 with rclpy.time.Time(). On a nominal one-second timer it publishes angular z from atan2 and linear x as 0.5 times translation distance. The period and gains are source settings, not measurements. Transform failures are logged and return without an explicit zero-velocity stop. No obstacle check or speed clamp is present. This node does not generate its required transforms, and a single source file is insufficient. ROS graph dependencies, shutdown behavior, hardware remappings and compatibility remain untested."
    }
  ],
